{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"af63a707c056b3e93871e9c0380b45934f77ab88b706c0f7f7c9298acc3640d5","digest":{"component_or_area":"rebar reconciler link-relation mapping","key_entities":["mapping_config.py","MappingLayer","outbound_links.py","_diff_links","_diff_link_removals","outbound_mutation_builders.py:285","config.py:77","RELATION_TO_JIRA_LINK","link_direction.JIRA_LINK_TO_RELATION","adapters/jira/backend.py:323","adapters/jira_datacenter/backend.py:527","effective_link_map","_resolve_link","value_maps.py:104","link_map"],"problem_keywords":["config-driven mapping","link-relation","rebar-to-jira","skip-not-approximate","ADD/REMOVE symmetry","config-aware attribution"],"propositions":["A config-driven link_map must govern both ADD (_diff_links) and REMOVE (_diff_link_removals) paths symmetrically via a single resolver (_resolve_link).","The reverse map must attribute remote links carrying overridden vendor types to their original relations by inverting the config link_map, preventing spurious drops when a relation is remapped.","A SKIP override must suppress both ADD and REMOVE emission, preserving the skip-not-approximate invariant (never invent an approximate link).","Undeclared link types outside a declared link_types vocabulary must fail closed via config.validate(), raising MappingConfigError.","ADD composes the config override link_type with the built-in swap tuple component; REMOVE emits using the actual remote vendor_type (which becomes the overridden type when remapped)."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787486864975756001,"uuid":"449bd3c8